{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>ויפל</b> Three times in the Masorah: ויפל עליו וימות · ויפל בקרב מחנהו · ויפל ה' אלהים תרדמה. As stated in the Midrash: more than the righteous kill them through eating, the wicked kill them through descent — he descends and falls upon their heads, and this is ויפל עליו וימות · ויפל ה' אלהים תרדמה. As stated in the Midrash: the righteous eat and die immediately; the wicked descend to their beds and linger up to thirty days. And this is ויפל ה' אלהים תרדמה — for a tardemah fell upon them, and they slept the sleep of eternity."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {0 "The Hebrew text contains apparent repetition of 'כדאיתא במררש' and then 'כדאיתא במדרש'; translated hyper-literally preserving both occurrences. 'מררש' appears to be a variant or scribal form of 'מדרש'; rendered as 'Midrash' in both instances."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:23:50.254140197Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}